  - Pulls up to `maxDrain` items using `xQueueReceive(_jobQueue, &entry, 0)`.
  - If `urgentOnly && !entry->options.urgent`, defers the entry to `deferred[deferredCount++]`.
  - Otherwise, wraps the job in `FetchGuard` / `FetchContext`, invokes `entry->job(ctx);`, and immediately calls `delete entry;`.
  - Re-queues any deferred items via `xQueueSend(_jobQueue, &deferred[i], 0)`.
- In `DataManager::~DataManager()`:
  - Deletes `_workerTask`.
  - Drains any remaining jobs from `_jobQueue` via `xQueueReceive` and calls `delete entry;`.
  - Deletes the queue via `vQueueDelete(_jobQueue)`.

